# Force LF line endings in the repository regardless of a contributor's local
# core.autocrlf setting (checking out with CRLF is harmless for TS/JS, but
# fatal for start.sh - a `#!/usr/bin/env bash^M` shebang fails to run on
# Linux/macOS with a "bad interpreter" error). Git still checks these files
# out with the OS's native line endings on Windows unless a tool explicitly
# needs LF (e.g. an editor respecting .gitattributes), but the *stored*
# blob - what `git clone`/GitHub Actions/Docker builds actually see - is
# always LF, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.bat text eol=crlf
